                                                  \setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
                                                  \begin{document}$${N}^{-2}=-\frac{g}{{\rho }_{0}}\frac{\partial \rho }{\partial z}$$\end{document}N−2=−gρ0∂ρ∂z, ρ represents the potential density, ρ0 is the reference density, and ε is the diagnosed kinetic energy dissipation rate. The buoyancy flux is related to the turbulence ε through the constant efficiency factor Г69 The expression for ε on each layer, which is derived from relevant physical principles, is as follows:7\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
